<title>UK: Sudan becomes 49th member of ISO.</title>
<headline>Sudan becomes 49th member of ISO.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sudan has become a party to the 1992 International Sugar Agreement, making it the 49th member of the International Sugar Organization (ISO), the ISO said in a statement on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Sudan became party to the Agreement on May 9.</p>
<p>Sudan is a modest producer on a world scale, producing around 500,000 tonnes of sugar raw value annually during the past five years, the ISO said.</p>
<p>It is self-sufficient in sugar and exports small, variable quantities to Middle East and African nations.</p>
<p>The ISO said Sudan was the organization's tenth new member since early 1994. The last two new members were the Philippines and Costa Rica. Both joined the ISO in October 1996.</p>
<p>-- Jeremy Smith, London Newsroom +44 171 542 8064</p>
